prompt:
Here are the template signs, each with the question that finds it. Yes to a question means the sign is there.

- Purple-to-blue or violet-to-pink gradients: Does a background, card, button, or active navigation item have a purple-to-blue or violet-to-pink gradient fill?
- Gradient text in headings, numbers, or the logo: Is a heading, a number, or the logo filled with a color gradient instead of one solid color?
- Colored glows around elements: Does a colored glow or a blurred colored halo surround a card, button, pill, icon, or emoji?
- Color washes and blurred blobs behind content: Is there a radial color wash, a blurred color blob, an orb, a decorative grid, or a glowing line behind the content or the hero?
- Neon or bright colored borders: Does a card, panel, or input have a neon or bright colored border?
- Many near-identical tints of one hue for text: Is the text on the screen set in four or more near-identical tints of one hue, such as several lavenders?
- Every element highlighted: Is the accent color or a highlight applied to so many elements on the screen that none of them stands out?
- Glass cards with an inner highlight and a colored shadow: Is a card drawn as frosted glass, with a white inner highlight along its edge and a colored shadow?
- Headings at weight 800 or 900: Is a heading set in an extra-bold or black weight?
- Uppercase labels with wide tracking: Is a label or other short line, such as a section name, a stat title, or a line above the hero headline, set in uppercase with wide letterspacing?
- Too many type sizes and weights on one screen: Does one screen show six or more different text sizes, or three or more weights?
- Numbers in mixed formats: Do numbers of the same kind on one screen appear in mixed formats, such as an amount with cents next to an amount without, or one number padded with a leading zero next to others that are not?
- Negative letter spacing on small text: Is small text, such as body text, captions, or labels, set so tight that its letters nearly touch?
- Italic used for emphasis in interface text: Is italic used to emphasize words in labels, buttons, or other short interface text?
- Emoji as icons or status: Is an emoji used as a navigation icon, as decoration on a label, or as a status marker?
- Emoji inside pills and counts: Does a pill, badge, or count hold an emoji next to its number?
- Icons in many sizes and colors: Do the icons on one screen come in several sizes, stroke weights, or colors?
- Icons nudged off the column: In a list or menu, do the icons, or the text after them, visibly step out of one vertical column?
- Sparkle icon as decoration: Is a sparkle icon or sparkle emoji used as decoration?
- Glowing pills for counts and status: Is a count, plan name, keyboard shortcut, or status shown in a pill that glows?
- PRO, New, and Beta badges everywhere: Do two or more elements on one screen carry a badge such as PRO, New, or Beta?
- Every element a full pill: Are most of the controls and containers on the screen, such as fields, buttons, and cards, drawn with fully rounded pill ends?
- Rainbow, glowing, or pill-shaped chart bars: Does a chart have bars in rainbow colors, glowing bars, bars with fully rounded ends, or day labels in uppercase?
- Every chart in shades of the accent: Is every series of a chart or stacked bar drawn in a shade of the accent color, so that no series leads?
- Sparklines on every stat card: Does every stat card in a row carry a sparkline, a tally, or a set of mini bars?
- Equal cards side by side with the same chart: Does a dashboard row hold equal cards side by side, each with the same chart or the same layout?
- Gradient logo tile with a sparkle: Is the logo a gradient tile with a sparkle, next to a wordmark filled with a gradient?
- Logo mark as a glossy orb: Is the logo mark a glossy orb, a gradient ball, or a glowing dot?
- Pill badge above the headline: Does a pill-shaped badge sit directly above the hero headline?
- Hero stacked on one centered axis: Are the hero headline, its text, its buttons, and a picture below them all stacked on one centered axis?
- Three or more buttons in the hero: Does the hero have three or more buttons, or chips or avatars stacked under its buttons?
- Feature cards with an emoji and a bold title: Is there a row of feature cards, each with an emoji, a bold title, and one line of text?
- Glossy 3D blob as the hero visual: Is the hero visual a glossy 3D blob, an orb, a liquid chrome shape, or a purple nebula?
- Stock robots, glowing brains, and holograms: Does a visual on the page show a stock robot, a glowing brain, circuit lines, or a hologram?
- Image that does not blend into the page: Does an image sit on the page as a box with a hard edge, on a background, such as a different black, that almost matches the page and does not?
- A visual on every section: Does every section of the page have its own decorative visual?
- Neutral dark template look: Is the page a near-black gray ground with white text in a stock neutral sans serif, the brand color on only one button, and no other color or element of its own?
- Empty box or generic picture as the hero visual: Is the hero visual empty, a placeholder, or a stock picture?

